    "settings.typesafe.unreachable": "Could not check — zo did not answer.",
    "settings.typesafe.shadowSummary": "Judges a task's difficulty, risk and intent, and a few facts about it. When on, a judgment it is sure of feeds into choosing the model that fits the task.",
    "settings.typesafe.recallSummary": "Judges how well the notes memory search found fit the request at hand. When on, the best-fitting notes are read first and unrelated ones are left out.",
    "settings.typesafe.skillsSummary": "Ranks the installed skills when the agent searches for one. Shadow mode records the ranking and hands back the word match.",
    "settings.typesafe.browserSummary": "Picks the button or link to press next on a web page. When on, a stopped automation and a goal-driven run press what it picked.",
    "settings.typesafe.emulator": "Phone automation",
    "settings.typesafe.emulatorSummary": "Picks the control to press next on a phone screen (iOS or Android). When on, a goal-driven run presses what it picked.",
    "settings.typesafe.emulatorHint": "Picks the one control to press next on a phone screen (iOS or Android). When on, it presses what it picked, but only numbers checked again against the screen, and it verifies the result with the confirmation you supplied. What is sent is the accessibility text of the numbered controls, the goal, and the platform and device identity, to api.typesafe.ai. Separate from the browser and desktop settings, it works only once you turn this feature on yourself.",
    "settings.typesafe.cover": "Uncovering a covered target",
    "settings.typesafe.coverSummary": "When the place to press is covered by another window, judges what covers it and what to do first. When on, it brings the target's window to the front or moves it clear as judged, checks again, and presses.",
    "settings.typesafe.coverHint": "Asks only when a place a press by number was going to land on is covered by another window. What is sent is the app name, layer, size and position of the target's window and of the windows over it (at most 12), and how much is covered — never a window title, screen text or a picture of the screen. The only window it moves is the target's own (to the front, or aside); what covers it is never read, closed or moved. When what covers it looks like a system alert, a permission request or a dialog waiting for an answer, or when the judgment is unsure, the hand stops and asks you in one line; when no answer comes within 1.5 seconds, it goes on as it does with no judgment. Under Record only, and when off, it brings the target's window to the front with no judgment and moves it if it is still covered (another app's floating window is left to you).",
    "settings.typesafe.desktopSummary": "Picks the control to press next in a desktop app. When on, a goal-driven run presses what it picked.",
    "settings.typesafe.stallSummary": "Judges why a worker that went quiet stopped. When on, the cause is passed to the coordinator, and a passing API error has the work carry on.",
    "settings.typesafe.placementSummary": "Judges whether a worker just started belongs in a tab, a split or the background. When on, the worker is placed where it judged.",
